{"$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/guitaripod/wwdc-sessions/master/schema/transcript.schema.json", "id": "wwdc2019-425", "language": "eng", "source": "https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2019/425", "wordCount": 2697, "segments": [{"start": 14.0, "text": "Good morning."}, {"start": 15.0, "text": "My name's Dan Klingler."}, {"start": 17.0, "text": "And, I'm a software engineer on"}, {"start": 18.0, "text": "the audio team here at Apple."}, {"start": 19.0, "text": "And, today I'm really excited to"}, {"start": 22.0, "text": "talk to you about training sound"}, {"start": 24.0, "text": "classification models in Create"}, {"start": 26.0, "text": "ML."}, {"start": 28.0, "text": "So, before we start, we might"}, {"start": 30.0, "text": "want to ask the question what is"}, {"start": 32.0, "text": "sound classification, and how"}, {"start": 34.0, "text": "might it be useful in your"}, {"start": 36.0, "text": "application?"}, {"start": 38.0, "text": "Sound classification is the task"}, {"start": 41.0, "text": "of taking a sound, and placing"}, {"start": 43.0, "text": "it into one of many categories."}, {"start": 45.0, "text": "But, if you think about it,"}, {"start": 47.0, "text": "there are many different ways"}, {"start": 49.0, "text": "that we can categorize sound."}, {"start": 51.0, "text": "One way might be to think about"}, {"start": 53.0, "text": "the object that makes the sound."}, {"start": 55.0, "text": "So, in this example, we have the"}, {"start": 57.0, "text": "sound of guitar, or the sound of"}, {"start": 59.0, "text": "drums."}, {"start": 60.0, "text": "And, it's really the acoustical"}, {"start": 62.0, "text": "properties of that object which"}, {"start": 63.0, "text": "are different, and allow us as"}, {"start": 65.0, "text": "humans to disambiguate these"}, {"start": 66.0, "text": "sounds."}, {"start": 69.0, "text": "But, a second way we could think"}, {"start": 70.0, "text": "about sound classification is"}, {"start": 73.0, "text": "where the sound comes from, and"}, {"start": 75.0, "text": "if you've ever gone on a hike,"}, {"start": 76.0, "text": "or been in the middle of a busy"}, {"start": 78.0, "text": "city, you'll understand that the"}, {"start": 80.0, "text": "texture of the sound around you"}, {"start": 82.0, "text": "is very different, even though"}, {"start": 85.0, "text": "there's not one particular sound"}, {"start": 86.0, "text": "that stands out, necessarily."}, {"start": 91.0, "text": "And, a third way we could think"}, {"start": 92.0, "text": "about sound classification, is"}, {"start": 94.0, "text": "by looking at the attributes of"}, {"start": 96.0, "text": "the sound, or the properties of"}, {"start": 97.0, "text": "the sound."}, {"start": 98.0, "text": "And so in this example, a baby's"}, {"start": 101.0, "text": "laugh versus a baby's cry."}, {"start": 104.0, "text": "Both come from the same source,"}, {"start": 106.0, "text": "but the properties of the sound"}, {"start": 107.0, "text": "are very different."}, {"start": 108.0, "text": "And, this allows us to tell the"}, {"start": 110.0, "text": "difference between these sounds."}, {"start": 113.0, "text": "Now, as app developers, you all"}, {"start": 116.0, "text": "have different apps, and you"}, {"start": 118.0, "text": "might have your different use"}, {"start": 119.0, "text": "case for sound classification."}, {"start": 122.0, "text": "And, wouldn't it be great if you"}, {"start": 124.0, "text": "could train your own model,"}, {"start": 126.0, "text": "tailor-made for your own"}, {"start": 127.0, "text": "application's use case?"}, {"start": 131.0, "text": "And, you can do that today using"}, {"start": 133.0, "text": "the Create ML app, which is"}, {"start": 135.0, "text": "built right into Xcode."}, {"start": 136.0, "text": "This is the simplest way to"}, {"start": 138.0, "text": "train a sound classifier model."}, {"start": 142.0, "text": "To train a sound classifier,"}, {"start": 145.0, "text": "you'll first provide labeled"}, {"start": 147.0, "text": "audio data to Create ML, in the"}, {"start": 149.0, "text": "form of audio files."}, {"start": 152.0, "text": "Then, Create ML will train a"}, {"start": 155.0, "text": "sound classifier model on your"}, {"start": 157.0, "text": "custom data."}, {"start": 159.0, "text": "And then, you can take that"}, {"start": 161.0, "text": "sound classifier, and use it"}, {"start": 163.0, "text": "right in your application."}, {"start": 165.0, "text": "And, I'd love to show you this"}, {"start": 166.0, "text": "process in action today, with a"}, {"start": 169.0, "text": "demo."}, {"start": 180.0, "text": "So, to start, I'm going to"}, {"start": 182.0, "text": "launch the Create ML app, which"}, {"start": 184.0, "text": "you can find bundled with your"}, {"start": 185.0, "text": "Xcode installation."}, {"start": 188.0, "text": "We're going to be creating a new"}, {"start": 190.0, "text": "document, and select Sound from"}, {"start": 193.0, "text": "the template chooser."}, {"start": 197.0, "text": "We'll click Next, and name our"}, {"start": 200.0, "text": "project MySoundClassifier."}, {"start": 203.0, "text": "Let's save this project to our"}, {"start": 205.0, "text": "Documents directory."}, {"start": 207.0, "text": "Once the Create ML app launches,"}, {"start": 210.0, "text": "you'll see this home screen, and"}, {"start": 212.0, "text": "the Input tab is selected on the"}, {"start": 213.0, "text": "left."}, {"start": 216.0, "text": "This is where we'll provide our"}, {"start": 217.0, "text": "training data to the Create ML"}, {"start": 219.0, "text": "app, in order to train our"}, {"start": 220.0, "text": "custom model."}, {"start": 223.0, "text": "You'll see some other tabs"}, {"start": 225.0, "text": "across the top here."}, {"start": 226.0, "text": "Like Training, Validation, and"}, {"start": 228.0, "text": "Testing."}, {"start": 229.0, "text": "And, these allow us to view some"}, {"start": 230.0, "text": "statistics on the accuracy of"}, {"start": 232.0, "text": "our model for each of these"}, {"start": 233.0, "text": "stages of training."}, {"start": 235.0, "text": "And, finally, the Output tab is"}, {"start": 238.0, "text": "where we'll expect to find our"}, {"start": 239.0, "text": "model after it's been trained."}, {"start": 242.0, "text": "And, we can also interact with"}, {"start": 243.0, "text": "our model in real time."}, {"start": 246.0, "text": "Now, today, I'm going to be"}, {"start": 247.0, "text": "training a musical instrument"}, {"start": 249.0, "text": "classifier. And, I've brought some"}, {"start": 251.0, "text": "instruments with me that we can"}, {"start": 253.0, "text": "try."}, {"start": 254.0, "text": "I have a TrainingData directory"}, {"start": 256.0, "text": "that we can open, and take a"}, {"start": 258.0, "text": "look at some of the sound files"}, {"start": 259.0, "text": "I've collected."}, {"start": 262.0, "text": "These contain recordings from an"}, {"start": 265.0, "text": "acoustic guitar, for example, or"}, {"start": 267.0, "text": "cowbell, or shaker."}, {"start": 270.0, "text": "To train our model, all we need"}, {"start": 273.0, "text": "to do is drag this directory"}, {"start": 276.0, "text": "straight into Create ML."}, {"start": 278.0, "text": "Create ML has figured out that"}, {"start": 281.0, "text": "we have a total of 49 sound"}, {"start": 283.0, "text": "files we're going to be using"}, {"start": 284.0, "text": "today. And, that spans 7 different"}, {"start": 287.0, "text": "classes."}, {"start": 290.0, "text": "All we need to do is press the"}, {"start": 292.0, "text": "Train button, and our model will"}, {"start": 293.0, "text": "begin training."}, {"start": 295.0, "text": "Now, the first thing Create ML"}, {"start": 297.0, "text": "is going to be doing when"}, {"start": 298.0, "text": "training this model is walking"}, {"start": 300.0, "text": "through each of the sound files"}, {"start": 302.0, "text": "we provided, and extracting"}, {"start": 303.0, "text": "audio features across the entire"}, {"start": 306.0, "text": "file."}, {"start": 307.0, "text": "And, once it's collected all"}, {"start": 308.0, "text": "these audio features, it will"}, {"start": 310.0, "text": "begin the process you're seeing"}, {"start": 311.0, "text": "now, which is where the model"}, {"start": 313.0, "text": "weights are updating"}, {"start": 314.0, "text": "iteratively."}, {"start": 317.0, "text": "As the model weights are"}, {"start": 318.0, "text": "updating, you can see that the"}, {"start": 319.0, "text": "performance is increasing, and"}, {"start": 322.0, "text": "our accuracy is moving towards"}, {"start": 324.0, "text": "100%, which is a good sign that"}, {"start": 326.0, "text": "our model is converging."}, {"start": 328.0, "text": "Now, if you think about the"}, {"start": 330.0, "text": "sounds we've collected today,"}, {"start": 331.0, "text": "they're fairly distinct, like"}, {"start": 333.0, "text": "cowbell and acoustic guitar"}, {"start": 335.0, "text": "sound fairly different."}, {"start": 336.0, "text": "And so, this particular model"}, {"start": 337.0, "text": "we've trained is able to do a"}, {"start": 338.0, "text": "really good job with the sounds,"}, {"start": 340.0, "text": "as you can see, on both the"}, {"start": 342.0, "text": "training and the validation"}, {"start": 343.0, "text": "sets."}, {"start": 344.0, "text": "The testing pane is a good place"}, {"start": 348.0, "text": "to provide a large data set that"}, {"start": 350.0, "text": "you might have for benchmarking."}, {"start": 353.0, "text": "The Create ML app allows you to"}, {"start": 355.0, "text": "train multiple models at the"}, {"start": 357.0, "text": "same time."}, {"start": 358.0, "text": "And, potentially provide"}, {"start": 360.0, "text": "different sets of training data."}, {"start": 361.0, "text": "And so, the testing pane is a"}, {"start": 363.0, "text": "great place if you want to"}, {"start": 365.0, "text": "provide a common benchmark for"}, {"start": 366.0, "text": "all those different model"}, {"start": 367.0, "text": "configurations you're training."}, {"start": 370.0, "text": "Finally, as we make our way to"}, {"start": 372.0, "text": "the Output tab, you'll see a UI"}, {"start": 374.0, "text": "that shows how we can interact"}, {"start": 376.0, "text": "with our model."}, {"start": 377.0, "text": "Now, I've collected one other"}, {"start": 379.0, "text": "file that I didn't include in my"}, {"start": 381.0, "text": "training set."}, {"start": 382.0, "text": "And, I've placed this in the"}, {"start": 384.0, "text": "TestingData directory."}, {"start": 385.0, "text": "When I drag that directory into"}, {"start": 388.0, "text": "the UI, you can see it"}, {"start": 390.0, "text": "recognizes a file called"}, {"start": 391.0, "text": "classification test."}, {"start": 394.0, "text": "As we scroll through this file,"}, {"start": 397.0, "text": "it appears that Create ML has"}, {"start": 399.0, "text": "classified the first second or"}, {"start": 400.0, "text": "so of this file as background"}, {"start": 402.0, "text": "noise."}, {"start": 403.0, "text": "Then, speech for the next couple"}, {"start": 405.0, "text": "seconds, and finally shaker."}, {"start": 410.0, "text": "But, let's find out if we agree"}, {"start": 412.0, "text": "with this classification."}, {"start": 414.0, "text": "And, we can listen to this file"}, {"start": 415.0, "text": "right here in the UI."}, {"start": 418.0, "text": "Test, 1, 2, 3."}, {"start": 430.0, "text": "So, it seems at least on the"}, {"start": 432.0, "text": "file that we've collected, that"}, {"start": 434.0, "text": "this model seems to be"}, {"start": 435.0, "text": "performing reasonably."}, {"start": 437.0, "text": "Now, what would be even better,"}, {"start": 439.0, "text": "is if we could interact with"}, {"start": 440.0, "text": "this model live."}, {"start": 442.0, "text": "And, to do that, we've added a"}, {"start": 444.0, "text": "button here that has Record"}, {"start": 446.0, "text": "Microphone."}, {"start": 448.0, "text": "And, once I begin recording, my"}, {"start": 450.0, "text": "Mac will begin feeding the"}, {"start": 452.0, "text": "built-in microphone data into"}, {"start": 454.0, "text": "the model we've just trained."}, {"start": 463.0, "text": "So, what you can see is, anytime"}, {"start": 465.0, "text": "I'm speaking, the model's"}, {"start": 467.0, "text": "recognizing speech with high"}, {"start": 468.0, "text": "confidence."}, {"start": 469.0, "text": "And, as I quiet down, you can"}, {"start": 471.0, "text": "see the model settle back down"}, {"start": 473.0, "text": "into a background state."}, {"start": 477.0, "text": "And, I brought a few instruments"}, {"start": 478.0, "text": "with me so that we can play"}, {"start": 479.0, "text": "along and see if the model can"}, {"start": 480.0, "text": "recognize them."}, {"start": 482.0, "text": "Let's start with a shaker."}, {"start": 492.0, "text": "I've also brought my trusty"}, {"start": 493.0, "text": "cowbell."}, {"start": 500.0, "text": "More cowbell!"}, {"start": 502.0, "text": "Well, the people have spoken."}, {"start": 503.0, "text": "More cowbell."}, {"start": 504.0, "text": "There you have it."}, {"start": 510.0, "text": "And, I also brought my acoustic"}, {"start": 512.0, "text": "guitar with me here today, so we"}, {"start": 514.0, "text": "can try some of this as well."}, {"start": 518.0, "text": "I can start with some"}, {"start": 519.0, "text": "single-note lines."}, {"start": 527.0, "text": "And then, we can try some chords"}, {"start": 528.0, "text": "as well."}, {"start": 545.0, "text": "So, that seemed to be working"}, {"start": 547.0, "text": "pretty well, and I think that's"}, {"start": 548.0, "text": "something we can work with."}, {"start": 550.0, "text": "So, I can stop the recording"}, {"start": 551.0, "text": "now."}, {"start": 552.0, "text": "And, in the Create ML app, I'm"}, {"start": 554.0, "text": "able to scroll back through this"}, {"start": 555.0, "text": "recording, and take a look at"}, {"start": 557.0, "text": "any of the segments that we've"}, {"start": 558.0, "text": "been analyzing so far."}, {"start": 561.0, "text": "This might be a great place to"}, {"start": 562.0, "text": "check if there are any"}, {"start": 563.0, "text": "anomalies, or things that it"}, {"start": 564.0, "text": "didn't get correct, and maybe we"}, {"start": 566.0, "text": "can clip some parts of this file"}, {"start": 568.0, "text": "to use, as part of our training"}, {"start": 569.0, "text": "set to improve the performance"}, {"start": 571.0, "text": "of our model."}, {"start": 573.0, "text": "And, finally, when we're happy"}, {"start": 575.0, "text": "that our model is performing the"}, {"start": 576.0, "text": "way we'd like, we can simply"}, {"start": 578.0, "text": "drag this model to our desktop,"}, {"start": 580.0, "text": "where we can integrate it into"}, {"start": 581.0, "text": "our application."}, {"start": 583.0, "text": "And, that's training a sound"}, {"start": 584.0, "text": "classifier in the Create ML app"}, {"start": 587.0, "text": "in under a minute, with zero"}, {"start": 588.0, "text": "lines of code."}, {"start": 599.0, "text": "So, you saw during the demo,"}, {"start": 601.0, "text": "there's some things to consider"}, {"start": 602.0, "text": "when collecting your training"}, {"start": 604.0, "text": "data."}, {"start": 605.0, "text": "And, the first thing you'll"}, {"start": 606.0, "text": "notice is how I collected this"}, {"start": 608.0, "text": "data in directories."}, {"start": 611.0, "text": "All the sounds that come from a"}, {"start": 612.0, "text": "guitar are placed in the Guitar"}, {"start": 615.0, "text": "directory."}, {"start": 616.0, "text": "And, likewise with a file like"}, {"start": 619.0, "text": "Drums or Background."}, {"start": 621.0, "text": "Now, let's talk about the"}, {"start": 622.0, "text": "background class for a minute."}, {"start": 625.0, "text": "Even though we're training a"}, {"start": 626.0, "text": "musical instrument classifier,"}, {"start": 628.0, "text": "you still need to consider what"}, {"start": 630.0, "text": "might happen if there's not any"}, {"start": 631.0, "text": "musical instruments being"}, {"start": 633.0, "text": "played, and if you only trained"}, {"start": 635.0, "text": "your model on musical"}, {"start": 636.0, "text": "instruments, but then fed it"}, {"start": 638.0, "text": "background data."}, {"start": 639.0, "text": "That's data it's never seen"}, {"start": 640.0, "text": "before."}, {"start": 641.0, "text": "And so, make sure that when"}, {"start": 643.0, "text": "you're training a sound"}, {"start": 644.0, "text": "classifier, if you expect your"}, {"start": 645.0, "text": "model to work in situations"}, {"start": 648.0, "text": "where there's background noise,"}, {"start": 650.0, "text": "to provide that as part of the"}, {"start": 651.0, "text": "class as well."}, {"start": 655.0, "text": "Now, suppose you had a file that"}, {"start": 657.0, "text": "was called sounds."}, {"start": 659.0, "text": "And, the file started at the"}, {"start": 661.0, "text": "beginning with drums, and then"}, {"start": 663.0, "text": "transitioned to background"}, {"start": 664.0, "text": "noise, and then finally ended"}, {"start": 667.0, "text": "with guitar."}, {"start": 669.0, "text": "This file, as is, is not going"}, {"start": 673.0, "text": "to be useful for dragging"}, {"start": 675.0, "text": "directly in the Create ML app."}, {"start": 677.0, "text": "And, that's because this sound"}, {"start": 678.0, "text": "contains multiple sound classes"}, {"start": 680.0, "text": "in one file."}, {"start": 683.0, "text": "Remember, you have to use"}, {"start": 685.0, "text": "labeled directories to train"}, {"start": 686.0, "text": "your model, and so the best"}, {"start": 688.0, "text": "thing to do in this situation"}, {"start": 689.0, "text": "would be to split this file into"}, {"start": 691.0, "text": "three, and name them drums,"}, {"start": 693.0, "text": "guitar, and background."}, {"start": 695.0, "text": "This is going to have a lot"}, {"start": 698.0, "text": "better performance when training"}, {"start": 699.0, "text": "your model, if you split your"}, {"start": 700.0, "text": "files this way."}, {"start": 704.0, "text": "A few other considerations when"}, {"start": 706.0, "text": "collecting audio data."}, {"start": 709.0, "text": "First, we want to insure that"}, {"start": 711.0, "text": "the data you're collecting"}, {"start": 713.0, "text": "matches a real-world audio"}, {"start": 714.0, "text": "environment."}, {"start": 715.0, "text": "So, remember that if your app is"}, {"start": 719.0, "text": "intended to work in a variety of"}, {"start": 721.0, "text": "rooms or acoustic scenarios, you"}, {"start": 723.0, "text": "can either collect data in those"}, {"start": 724.0, "text": "acoustic scenarios, or consider"}, {"start": 726.0, "text": "even simulating those rooms,"}, {"start": 728.0, "text": "using a technique called"}, {"start": 729.0, "text": "convolution."}, {"start": 732.0, "text": "Another important thing to"}, {"start": 734.0, "text": "consider is the on-device"}, {"start": 736.0, "text": "microphone processing."}, {"start": 737.0, "text": "You might check out AV audio"}, {"start": 740.0, "text": "session modes to select"}, {"start": 743.0, "text": "different modes of microphone"}, {"start": 744.0, "text": "processing in your application,"}, {"start": 746.0, "text": "and select the one which is best"}, {"start": 747.0, "text": "suited for your app, or"}, {"start": 749.0, "text": "potentially matches the training"}, {"start": 751.0, "text": "data you've collected."}, {"start": 754.0, "text": "And a final point, is to be"}, {"start": 756.0, "text": "aware of the model architecture."}, {"start": 759.0, "text": "So, this is the sound classifier"}, {"start": 760.0, "text": "model, and it can do pretty well"}, {"start": 762.0, "text": "at classifying varieties of"}, {"start": 764.0, "text": "sounds."}, {"start": 765.0, "text": "But, this is not something that"}, {"start": 766.0, "text": "would be suitable for, say,"}, {"start": 768.0, "text": "training a full-on speech"}, {"start": 769.0, "text": "recognizer."}, {"start": 770.0, "text": "There are better tools for that"}, {"start": 772.0, "text": "job. So, make sure you're always"}, {"start": 773.0, "text": "using the right tool for the"}, {"start": 774.0, "text": "job."}, {"start": 777.0, "text": "So, now you have this ML model,"}, {"start": 780.0, "text": "and let's talk about how you can"}, {"start": 781.0, "text": "integrate it into your"}, {"start": 782.0, "text": "application."}, {"start": 785.0, "text": "And, to make it as easy as"}, {"start": 787.0, "text": "possible to run sound"}, {"start": 788.0, "text": "classification models in your"}, {"start": 790.0, "text": "app, we're also releasing a new"}, {"start": 791.0, "text": "framework called SoundAnalysis."}, {"start": 795.0, "text": "SoundAnalysis is a new"}, {"start": 797.0, "text": "high-level framework for"}, {"start": 799.0, "text": "analyzing sound."}, {"start": 801.0, "text": "It uses Core ML models, and it"}, {"start": 805.0, "text": "handles common audio operations"}, {"start": 807.0, "text": "internally, such as channel"}, {"start": 809.0, "text": "mapping, sample rate conversion,"}, {"start": 811.0, "text": "or reblocking."}, {"start": 815.0, "text": "And, let's take a look under the"}, {"start": 816.0, "text": "hood to see how SoundAnalysis"}, {"start": 818.0, "text": "works."}, {"start": 819.0, "text": "Now, the top section represents"}, {"start": 821.0, "text": "your application."}, {"start": 823.0, "text": "And, the bottom represents"}, {"start": 824.0, "text": "what's happening under the hood"}, {"start": 825.0, "text": "in SoundAnalysis."}, {"start": 827.0, "text": "The first thing you'll do is"}, {"start": 830.0, "text": "provide the model you just"}, {"start": 831.0, "text": "trained using Create ML to"}, {"start": 833.0, "text": "SoundAnalysis framework."}, {"start": 836.0, "text": "Then, your application will"}, {"start": 839.0, "text": "provide some audio that needs to"}, {"start": 841.0, "text": "be analyzed."}, {"start": 844.0, "text": "This audio will first hit a"}, {"start": 846.0, "text": "channel-mapping step, which"}, {"start": 848.0, "text": "ensures that if your model"}, {"start": 849.0, "text": "expects one channel of audio,"}, {"start": 852.0, "text": "like ours did here, that that's"}, {"start": 854.0, "text": "what's delivered to the model,"}, {"start": 856.0, "text": "even as a client, if you're"}, {"start": 857.0, "text": "delivering stereo data, for"}, {"start": 859.0, "text": "example."}, {"start": 862.0, "text": "The next step that happens is"}, {"start": 863.0, "text": "called sample rate conversion."}, {"start": 866.0, "text": "The model we trained natively"}, {"start": 868.0, "text": "operates on 16 kilohertz audio"}, {"start": 870.0, "text": "data."}, {"start": 871.0, "text": "And, this ensures that the audio"}, {"start": 873.0, "text": "that you provide gets converted"}, {"start": 875.0, "text": "to match the rate the model"}, {"start": 876.0, "text": "expects."}, {"start": 881.0, "text": "The final step that"}, {"start": 882.0, "text": "SoundAnalysis performs is an"}, {"start": 883.0, "text": "audio buffering operation."}, {"start": 886.0, "text": "Most of the models we're working"}, {"start": 887.0, "text": "with today require a fixed"}, {"start": 890.0, "text": "amount of audio data to process"}, {"start": 892.0, "text": "an analysis chunk."}, {"start": 894.0, "text": "And, oftentimes, the audio that"}, {"start": 896.0, "text": "you have as a client might be"}, {"start": 898.0, "text": "coming in at arbitrary sized"}, {"start": 900.0, "text": "buffers."}, {"start": 901.0, "text": "And, it's a lot of work to"}, {"start": 902.0, "text": "implement an efficient ring"}, {"start": 904.0, "text": "buffer that makes sure to"}, {"start": 905.0, "text": "deliver the correct size chunks"}, {"start": 907.0, "text": "of audio to your model."}, {"start": 909.0, "text": "And so, this step ensures that"}, {"start": 911.0, "text": "if the model expects around 1"}, {"start": 913.0, "text": "second of audio data, that that"}, {"start": 915.0, "text": "will always be what's delivered"}, {"start": 916.0, "text": "to the model."}, {"start": 918.0, "text": "And then, finally, after the"}, {"start": 920.0, "text": "data's delivered to the model,"}, {"start": 922.0, "text": "your app will receive a"}, {"start": 923.0, "text": "callback, containing the top"}, {"start": 925.0, "text": "classification results for that"}, {"start": 927.0, "text": "piece of audio."}, {"start": 928.0, "text": "Now, the good thing is, you"}, {"start": 931.0, "text": "don't really have to know any of"}, {"start": 932.0, "text": "this."}, {"start": 933.0, "text": "Just remember to take your"}, {"start": 935.0, "text": "audio, provide it to"}, {"start": 936.0, "text": "SoundAnalysis framework, and"}, {"start": 938.0, "text": "then handle the results in your"}, {"start": 940.0, "text": "application."}, {"start": 943.0, "text": "So, let's talk a little bit more"}, {"start": 945.0, "text": "about the results you'll expect"}, {"start": 946.0, "text": "to get from SoundAnalysis."}, {"start": 949.0, "text": "Audio is a stream, and it"}, {"start": 951.0, "text": "doesn't always have a beginning"}, {"start": 953.0, "text": "and end, like images do."}, {"start": 954.0, "text": "And, for this reason, the"}, {"start": 956.0, "text": "results that we're working with"}, {"start": 958.0, "text": "might look a little different."}, {"start": 960.0, "text": "Your results contain a time"}, {"start": 962.0, "text": "range, and this corresponds to"}, {"start": 964.0, "text": "the block of audio that was"}, {"start": 965.0, "text": "analyzed for that result."}, {"start": 968.0, "text": "In this example, the block size"}, {"start": 970.0, "text": "is specific to model"}, {"start": 971.0, "text": "architecture, and is around 1"}, {"start": 973.0, "text": "second, as you can see."}, {"start": 977.0, "text": "As you continue providing audio"}, {"start": 978.0, "text": "data to the model, you'll"}, {"start": 980.0, "text": "continue to receive results"}, {"start": 981.0, "text": "containing the top"}, {"start": 982.0, "text": "classifications for that block"}, {"start": 984.0, "text": "of audio that you analyzed."}, {"start": 987.0, "text": "Now, you might notice that this"}, {"start": 989.0, "text": "second result has overlapped the"}, {"start": 991.0, "text": "previous results by about 50%."}, {"start": 993.0, "text": "And, this is actually by design."}, {"start": 996.0, "text": "You want to make sure that every"}, {"start": 998.0, "text": "piece of audio that you're"}, {"start": 999.0, "text": "providing has the opportunity to"}, {"start": 1000.0, "text": "fall near the middle of an"}, {"start": 1002.0, "text": "analysis window."}, {"start": 1003.0, "text": "Otherwise, it might fall between"}, {"start": 1005.0, "text": "two analysis windows, and the"}, {"start": 1008.0, "text": "model performance might not be"}, {"start": 1009.0, "text": "as good."}, {"start": 1011.0, "text": "And so, the default is 50%"}, {"start": 1013.0, "text": "overlap on the analysis,"}, {"start": 1015.0, "text": "although it's configurable in"}, {"start": 1016.0, "text": "the API, if you have a use case"}, {"start": 1017.0, "text": "that requires otherwise."}, {"start": 1020.0, "text": "And, as you continue providing"}, {"start": 1022.0, "text": "audio data, you'll continue to"}, {"start": 1024.0, "text": "receive results."}, {"start": 1025.0, "text": "And, you can continue pushing"}, {"start": 1028.0, "text": "this data, and getting results"}, {"start": 1029.0, "text": "for as long as the audio stream"}, {"start": 1030.0, "text": "is active."}, {"start": 1035.0, "text": "Now, let's take a quick look at"}, {"start": 1038.0, "text": "the API provided by"}, {"start": 1039.0, "text": "SoundAnalysis Framework."}, {"start": 1043.0, "text": "Let's say we have an audio file,"}, {"start": 1044.0, "text": "and we want to analyze it using"}, {"start": 1047.0, "text": "the classifier we've just"}, {"start": 1048.0, "text": "trained here today."}, {"start": 1050.0, "text": "To start, we'll create an audio"}, {"start": 1052.0, "text": "file analyzer, and provide the"}, {"start": 1054.0, "text": "URL to the file we'd like to"}, {"start": 1056.0, "text": "analyze."}, {"start": 1058.0, "text": "Then, we'll create a"}, {"start": 1060.0, "text": "classifySoundRequest, and then"}, {"start": 1062.0, "text": "instantiate MySoundClassifier,"}, {"start": 1065.0, "text": "which is the model we trained"}, {"start": 1066.0, "text": "here."}, {"start": 1069.0, "text": "Then, we'll add this request to"}, {"start": 1071.0, "text": "our analyzer, and provide an"}, {"start": 1073.0, "text": "observer, which will handle the"}, {"start": 1075.0, "text": "results that the model will"}, {"start": 1076.0, "text": "produce."}, {"start": 1079.0, "text": "Finally, we'll analyze the file,"}, {"start": 1082.0, "text": "which will start scanning"}, {"start": 1083.0, "text": "through the file and producing"}, {"start": 1085.0, "text": "the results."}, {"start": 1089.0, "text": "Now, on your application side,"}, {"start": 1091.0, "text": "you'll need to make sure that"}, {"start": 1092.0, "text": "one of your classes implements"}, {"start": 1094.0, "text": "the SNResultsObserving protocol."}, {"start": 1097.0, "text": "This is how you'll receive"}, {"start": 1098.0, "text": "results from the framework."}, {"start": 1101.0, "text": "The first method you might"}, {"start": 1103.0, "text": "implement is request didProduce"}, {"start": 1105.0, "text": "result."}, {"start": 1106.0, "text": "This method will be called many"}, {"start": 1108.0, "text": "times, potentially."}, {"start": 1110.0, "text": "Once for each new observation"}, {"start": 1112.0, "text": "that's available."}, {"start": 1114.0, "text": "You might consider grabbing the"}, {"start": 1117.0, "text": "top classification result, and"}, {"start": 1119.0, "text": "the time range associated with"}, {"start": 1120.0, "text": "it."}, {"start": 1121.0, "text": "And, this is where the logic"}, {"start": 1122.0, "text": "would go in your application, to"}, {"start": 1124.0, "text": "handle the sound classification"}, {"start": 1126.0, "text": "event."}, {"start": 1129.0, "text": "Another method you'll be"}, {"start": 1130.0, "text": "interested in is request"}, {"start": 1132.0, "text": "didFailWithError."}, {"start": 1134.0, "text": "If analysis fails for any"}, {"start": 1135.0, "text": "reason, this method will be"}, {"start": 1137.0, "text": "called. And then, you shouldn't expect"}, {"start": 1139.0, "text": "to receive any more results from"}, {"start": 1140.0, "text": "this analyzer."}, {"start": 1142.0, "text": "Or, if the stream completes"}, {"start": 1144.0, "text": "successfully, at the end of the"}, {"start": 1146.0, "text": "file, for example, you'll"}, {"start": 1148.0, "text": "receive the request didComplete."}, {"start": 1153.0, "text": "So, let's recap what you've seen"}, {"start": 1155.0, "text": "today."}, {"start": 1157.0, "text": "You saw how you can train a"}, {"start": 1158.0, "text": "sound classifier in Create ML"}, {"start": 1161.0, "text": "using your own audio data."}, {"start": 1165.0, "text": "And, take that model and run it"}, {"start": 1167.0, "text": "on-device using SoundAnalysis"}, {"start": 1169.0, "text": "framework."}, {"start": 1172.0, "text": "For more information, check out"}, {"start": 1174.0, "text": "our sound classification article"}, {"start": 1176.0, "text": "on developer.apple.com."}, {"start": 1179.0, "text": "And, there you'll find an"}, {"start": 1180.0, "text": "example of how to perform sound"}, {"start": 1182.0, "text": "classification on your device's"}, {"start": 1184.0, "text": "built-in microphone, using AV"}, {"start": 1185.0, "text": "Audio Engine, just like the"}, {"start": 1187.0, "text": "musical instrument demo you saw"}, {"start": 1189.0, "text": "earlier."}, {"start": 1193.0, "text": "Thank you all for listening, and"}, {"start": 1194.0, "text": "I can't wait to see how you use"}, {"start": 1196.0, "text": "sound classification in your"}]}
